{
  "name": "moh505AgeDisaggregation",
  "version": "1.0",
  "tag": "",
  "description": "MOH 505 age-band aggregate: pivots the encounter-grain moh505ReportBase rows into one summary row per (location, age band), with every indicator counted as DISTINCT persons flagged positive (COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN flag > 0 THEN person_id END)) so a patient with several flagged encounters in the period counts once - the flat table is encounter-grain, the register counts cases. transFormDirectives pivot age_range into dc__age_range__0_to_4__<indicator> / dc__age_range__5_and_above__<indicator> columns keyed on location_id (report-processor-helpers tranform), which is the app contract the MOH-505 screen binds. Patient-list drill-downs generate from moh505PatientList joined per person.",
  "uses": [
    {
      "name": "moh505ReportBase",
      "version": "1.0",
      "type": "dataset_def"
    }
  ],
  "sources": [
    {
      "dataSet": "moh505ReportBase",
      "alias": "b"
    }
  ],
  "columns": [
